MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Peter, Paul and Mary feels like a natural next choice because the folk harmonies connect closely with my listening to Simon & Garfunkel, Jonathan Edwards, and Melanie.",
    "Carpenters Gold and Glen Campbell offer the melodic older songs I want to revisit, while Ultimate Hits connects with my interest in classic rock collections."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Adele and Shania Twain do not fit my current interest in older folk and classic hits; being familiar artists or offering a hits collection is not enough to make me choose them today.",
    "I cannot judge Greatest Hits, Vol. 1 and 2 without knowing the artist. Sinatra and Call Me Irresponsible have a plausible connection to Cheek to Cheek, but vocal standards are a secondary interest today."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to treat greatest-hits collections as interchangeable, although the artist and musical sound matter more to me than the compilation format.",
    "My interest in some contemporary pop seems to carry too much weight for what I want now: familiar older folk, melodic songs, and classic rock."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The connection among Simon & Garfunkel, Jonathan Edwards, and Melanie matters especially to me: folk-oriented songs and harmonies make Peter, Paul and Mary a stronger choice.",
    "My repeated interest in older hits collections matters more than any single album. Cheek to Cheek supports some standards recommendations, but it does not make them my first choice today."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in familiar songs and collections, but sometimes overlook the older folk and classic-hit sounds that make those collections appealing to me now."
}
